# Enlightened Confidant: the trigger checks "if you gained life this turn" when it would trigger (2 life from the lifelink
# attack), but the last part counts the life as the ability resolves. With the trigger on the stack at the end step, Bot1 casts
# Swords to Plowshares on its own Confidant and gains 2 more (4 in all): Wrath of God (mana value 4) surveilled into the
# graveyard now goes to hand, though it would not have with only the 2. The ability resolves although its source is gone.

[Bot1 Deck]
Plains
Black Lotus
Enlightened Confidant
Swords to Plowshares
Plains x3
Island
Wrath of God
Plains x11

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: White)
Bot1.Hand.Enlightened Confidant.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Attack(Enlightened Confidant)
[T3 Bot1.End]
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Swords to Plowshares.Cast(Enlightened Confidant)
Bot1.Arrange(| Wrath of God)
[T5 Bot1.Upkeep]

[Expect]
Bot1.Life = 24
Bot1.Hand = Island; Plains; Plains; Plains; Wrath of God
Bot1.Graveyard = Swords to Plowshares; Black Lotus
Exile = Enlightened Confidant
